# 13. Phase I — Install PostgreSQL and pgvector

PostgreSQL will store:

* Open WebUI accounts and chats
* Conversation history
* Document metadata
* Vector embeddings through pgvector
* Structured personal records
* Future reminder and audit records

Using PostgreSQL from the beginning avoids a later migration from Open WebUI’s default SQLite database. Open WebUI’s documentation recommends PostgreSQL for reliability and pgvector or another external vector database for scalable retrieval.

## 13.1 Check the available packages

Run:

```bash
sudo apt update
apt-cache policy postgresql
apt-cache search pgvector
```

Ubuntu includes PostgreSQL packages, and the PostgreSQL project supports Ubuntu 26.04 through its official package repository.

Attempt the Ubuntu packages first:

```bash
sudo apt install -y postgresql postgresql-contrib postgresql-18-pgvector
```

If `postgresql-18-pgvector` is not found, do not substitute an unknown package. Use the official PostgreSQL repository:

```bash
sudo apt install -y postgresql-common curl ca-certificates
sudo /usr/share/postgresql-common/pgdg/apt.postgresql.org.sh
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y postgresql-18 postgresql-client-18 postgresql-18-pgvector
```

## 13.2 Verify PostgreSQL

Run:

```bash
psql --version
sudo systemctl status postgresql
```

Expected major version:

```text
PostgreSQL 18
```

Check readiness:

```bash
pg_isready
```

Expected:

```text
accepting connections
```

## 13.3 Verify local-only networking

Run:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -tAc "SHOW listen_addresses;"
```

Expected:

```text
localhost
```

Also run:

```bash
sudo ss -ltnp | grep 5432
```

Acceptable addresses:

```text
127.0.0.1:5432
[::1]:5432
```

Unacceptable:

```text
0.0.0.0:5432
[::]:5432
```

If PostgreSQL listens publicly, stop and correct `listen_addresses` before continuing.

## 13.4 Generate the Open WebUI database password

Run:

```bash
DB_PASS=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
```

Do not close the terminal until the environment file is created later.

To verify that the variable exists without printing the secret:

```bash
echo "${#DB_PASS}"
```

Expected:

```text
64
```

## 13.5 Create the Open WebUI database and role

Check whether the role already exists:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -tAc "SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname='openwebui';"
```

On a new installation, this should return nothing.

Create the role and database:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -v dbpass="$DB_PASS" <<'SQL'
CREATE ROLE openwebui LOGIN PASSWORD :'dbpass';
CREATE DATABASE openwebui OWNER openwebui;
SQL
```

Enable pgvector:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -d openwebui -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;"
```

Verify:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -d openwebui -c "\dx"
```

The output should include:

```text
vector
```

## 13.6 Create the structured personal-data database

Generate passwords:

```bash
PERSONAL_OWNER_PASS=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
PERSONAL_READER_PASS=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
```

Create the database and roles:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql \
    -v ownerpass="$PERSONAL_OWNER_PASS" \
    -v readerpass="$PERSONAL_READER_PASS" <<'SQL'
CREATE ROLE personal_owner LOGIN PASSWORD :'ownerpass';
CREATE ROLE personal_reader LOGIN PASSWORD :'readerpass';
CREATE DATABASE personal_data OWNER personal_owner;
GRANT CONNECT ON DATABASE personal_data TO personal_reader;
SQL
```

Create the initial schema:

```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -d personal_data <<'SQL'
SET ROLE personal_owner;

CREATE TABLE restaurants (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    cuisine TEXT,
    visited_on DATE,
    city TEXT,
    state TEXT,
    rating NUMERIC(3,1),
    companions TEXT,
    notes TEXT,
    source_file TEXT,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX restaurants_name_lower_idx
    ON restaurants (LOWER(name));

CREATE INDEX restaurants_cuisine_lower_idx
    ON restaurants (LOWER(cuisine));

CREATE INDEX restaurants_visited_on_idx
    ON restaurants (visited_on);

CREATE TABLE investment_holdings (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    symbol TEXT NOT NULL,
    investment_name TEXT,
    quantity NUMERIC(24,8) NOT NULL,
    account_label TEXT,
    manually_verified BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    source_description TEXT,
    effective_date DATE NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX investment_holdings_symbol_idx
    ON investment_holdings (UPPER(symbol));

CREATE TABLE investment_price_snapshots (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    symbol TEXT NOT NULL,
    price NUMERIC(24,8) NOT NULL,
    currency TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'USD',
    source_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    source_reference TEXT,
    observed_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    retrieved_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX investment_prices_symbol_time_idx
    ON investment_price_snapshots (UPPER(symbol), observed_at DESC);

CREATE TABLE reminders (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    reminder_text TEXT NOT NULL,
    due_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    timezone TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'America/Denver',
    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
    delivery_method TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'local',
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    completed_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);

CREATE INDEX reminders_due_status_idx
    ON reminders (status, due_at);

RESET ROLE;

GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA public TO personal_reader;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO personal_reader;

ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR ROLE personal_owner
    IN SCHEMA public
    GRANT SELECT ON TABLES TO personal_reader;
SQL
```

The future AI query tool will use `personal_reader`, which has read-only access.

The AI will not receive the `personal_owner` password.

