# 19. Memory design

Reliable memory requires more than storing chat history.

Use three layers.

## 19.1 Full conversations

Stored automatically in PostgreSQL through Open WebUI.

These are the historical record.

## 19.2 Proposed memory

After an important conversation, ask the assistant to produce a proposed memory note.

Save it under:

```text
/srv/local-ai/proposed/memory/
```

or:

```text
80_Memory/Proposed/
```

Review it for:

* False claims
* Missing context
* Incorrect dates
* Overgeneralizations
* Sensitive information
* Temporary facts presented as permanent

## 19.3 Approved memory

After review, move the corrected note into:

```text
80_Memory/Approved/
```

Then index it into:

```text
Personal Knowledge — Approved
```

Only approved memory should be treated as durable personal context.

The AI should never silently rewrite approved memory.

## 19.4 Superseding old information

Do not simply overwrite old important information.

Use metadata:

```yaml
supersedes: Older Note Name
last_verified: 2026-08-03
```

Mark the old note:

```yaml
status: superseded
superseded_by: New Note Name
```

This preserves history and reduces contradictions.

