# 23. Remote access from MacBook and phone — later phase

Do not open Open WebUI directly to the public internet.

Do not configure router port forwarding.

Do not use Open WebUI on a public IP.

The preferred later method is Tailscale:

```text
Ubuntu PC
MacBook
Phone
```

All three devices join the same private Tailscale network.

Then use Tailscale Serve to privately proxy the localhost Open WebUI interface. Do not use Tailscale Funnel, which publishes a service to the public internet.

Even through Tailscale:

* Keep Open WebUI authentication enabled.
* Use a strong password.
* Keep account signup disabled.
* Do not expose PostgreSQL or Ollama.
* Do not give other household devices access automatically.
* Do not add your wife’s computer unless there is a clear and deliberate reason.

Remote access should be added only after the local security tests and first external backup are complete.

