# 24. Restricted external information — later phase

General Open WebUI web search remains disabled.

External information should enter through a separate, narrow fetch service.

For example:

```text
get_approved_stock_quote(symbol)
get_weather_for_location(location)
retrieve_specific_public_page(approved_source, identifier)
```

The fetch service—not the language model—must enforce:

* HTTPS only
* GET requests only
* Exact hostname allowlist
* No IP-address URLs
* No private-network addresses
* No localhost access
* No file downloads
* No browser automation
* No JavaScript execution
* No forms
* No login sessions
* No cookies unless explicitly required
* No redirects to nonapproved domains
* Maximum response size
* Allowed content types
* Request and response logging
* Timeouts
* Rate limits

The model should never receive a generic function such as:

```text
open_any_url(url)
```

A trusted-site allowlist is stronger when implemented in the fetch service or network proxy, not merely written in the AI’s instructions.

Because many websites use multiple content-delivery and authentication domains, each approved source must be tested individually.

