# 25. Future tool gateway

After the core system passes every acceptance test, add a policy-enforced tool gateway.

n8n is one possible workflow host, but it should not be the source of security by itself. The actual restrictions come from:

* Narrow workflow definitions
* Restricted credentials
* Read-only database roles
* Service accounts
* Filesystem permissions
* Explicit approval gates
* Network allowlists
* Missing dangerous tools

## 25.1 Tools allowed to run automatically

Potential read-only tools:

```text
search_approved_knowledge
query_restaurants
read_investment_holdings
calculate_portfolio_from_verified_data
list_reminders
read_calendar
search_email_metadata
retrieve_approved_stock_price
```

## 25.2 Tools requiring approval

Potential state-changing tools:

```text
save_email_draft
create_calendar_event
create_reminder
write_report
store_proposed_memory
update_proposed_holdings
move_file_into_review_queue
```

The approval screen must show the exact proposed action and arguments.

## 25.3 Tools that should not exist

Do not create:

```text
send_email
delete_file
run_shell
run_python
install_software
browse_any_website
submit_form
make_purchase
place_trade
read_brokerage_account
change_permissions
edit_workflow
disable_security
access_other_computers
```

A model cannot invoke a tool that does not exist.

## 25.4 Credentials

Credentials remain in the workflow service or operating-system secret store.

The model receives:

* Tool name
* Accepted parameters
* Result

The model does not receive:

* OAuth refresh token
* Password
* API secret
* Database owner password
* Encryption key

## 25.5 Email design

Initial email capability:

```text
Read selected emails
Summarize them
Generate proposed replies in the chat
```

Later capability:

```text
Save a draft after approval
```

Absent capability:

```text
Send email
```

The email reader should request the narrowest scopes possible.

## 25.6 Calendar design

Initial calendar capability:

```text
Read today’s appointments
Summarize the schedule
```

Later capability:

```text
Propose an event
Create it only after approval
```

Absent capability:

```text
Delete or modify events without approval
```

## 25.7 Reminder design

A reminder request should produce a structured proposal:

```text
Reminder:
Due date:
Time:
Timezone:
Delivery method:
```

After approval, the tool inserts it into the reminder database.

A separate scheduler checks pending reminders.

The language model should not continuously run or independently decide when to notify you.

