# 26. Performance expectations on the current computer

## 26.1 HDD

The HDD will make these operations slower:

* Ubuntu startup
* Model loading
* PostgreSQL indexing
* Bulk document ingestion
* Reindexing
* Backup creation
* Large file retrieval

Once a model is loaded into GPU/RAM, text generation may be considerably faster than its initial load.

## 26.2 RTX 2070 SUPER

The 8 GB VRAM is appropriate for:

* Gemma 4 E4B
* EmbeddingGemma
* Some quantized models in the general 7B–9B range

It is restrictive for:

* Larger context windows
* 12B models fully on GPU
* 26B or 31B models
* Multiple models loaded simultaneously

## 26.3 Sixteen GB RAM

Sixteen GB is workable for the initial stack, but it is a significant constraint.

A future upgrade to 64 GB will help with:

* Larger models
* Longer context
* Bulk indexing
* Document extraction
* PostgreSQL caching
* Running n8n and auxiliary services
* Avoiding memory pressure

It will not make CPU-offloaded large models as fast as having adequate GPU VRAM.

## 26.4 Future SSD migration

Because all local-AI files are organized beneath:

```text
/srv/local-ai
```

a future migration can move this tree to a new encrypted SSD and remount it at the same path.

The highest-value items to place on SSD later are:

1. PostgreSQL data
2. pgvector index
3. Ollama models
4. Open WebUI application data
5. Frequently accessed Obsidian knowledge
6. Temporary document-extraction files

